  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 2.48,
      "end": 10.88,
      "text": "Excellent track by the American band called Rat. It is called Lack of Communication.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.88,
      "end": 201.14,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 201.14,
      "end": 208.21,
      "text": "And before that, Twisted Sister from an EP they had out some time ago which was called We're Not Gonna Take It. The track you hope is called The Kids Are Back.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 208.21,
      "end": 215.59,
      "text": "It is 8 minutes past 10. The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1. Mentions here for Paul Tinson and John Smart.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 215.59,
      "end": 220.59,
      "text": "And also the Zed Pals of James McKay in Perth in Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 221.68,
      "end": 224.48,
      "text": "Hello to Kenny Gilpin and Filthy Phil Thompson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 225.08,
      "end": 228.24,
      "text": "All from, I think it's Redburn, U-L-S-T-E-R.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 228.4,
      "end": 230.34,
      "text": "Tell Kenny that Elkie loves him.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 230.86,
      "end": 231.7,
      "text": "And Elkie wrote that.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 232.58,
      "end": 233.7,
      "text": "And she's in Belfast now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 236.13,
      "end": 238.79,
      "text": "Hello to a lady who's got a birthday on the 24th of December.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 238.99,
      "end": 244.43,
      "text": "She is the mother of Louise, I think it's pronounced Moya, M-A-W-E-R.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 244.61,
      "end": 245.31,
      "text": "Moya, maybe.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 245.87,
      "end": 247.13,
      "text": "Anyway, you know who you are.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 247.21,
      "end": 250.53,
      "text": "You're in Boothdown in Halifax, and Mum, have a happy birthday on the 24th.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 250.97,
      "end": 252.09,
      "text": "Louise, how are you?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 252.61,
      "end": 260.62,
      "text": "Twisted Sister track, especially for Helen Amos, who's in Roxburghshire in Scotland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 260.62,
      "end": 268.18,
      "text": "And also for her friends by the name of Joanna, Klinger, Sammy, Val, Isla, Leslie, and also Angus Young, and of course Paul Stanley of Kiss.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 273.17,
      "end": 275.45,
      "text": "This is a good single. It's by Warlock.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 275.77,
      "end": 285.37,
      "text": "...Rox from our repeat session by them. The track was called Don't You Ever Leave Me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 360.0,
      "end": 867.86,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 867.86,
      "end": 871.9,
      "text": "Before that, a single by Warlock out on Mausoleum called Without You.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 873.21,
      "end": 876.63,
      "text": "Mausoleum are German, rather. They come from the sort of Dusseldorf area.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 876.63,
      "end": 881.36,
      "text": "they're led by a very attractive lady called dorothy peff well i think it's only about 20",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 881.36,
      "end": 890.95,
      "text": "years of age she makes joan jett sound like city 19 minutes after 10 i mentioned here from a lady",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 890.95,
      "end": 894.39,
      "text": "who actually sent me a telephone number unfortunately i don't know how to use the phone",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 894.39,
      "end": 900.84,
      "text": "her name is sue a lightfoot of cottingley in bingley west yorkshire and she met a fella at",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.84,
      "end": 907.0,
      "text": "the queen's hall bradford on the 12th of october 1984 at the final hooligans gig of that year",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 907.0,
      "end": 908.44,
      "text": "which is nearly ended now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 909.28,
      "end": 910.98,
      "text": "We haven't got his name, actually,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 911.08,
      "end": 912.78,
      "text": "but he's from Harrogate in North Yorkshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 913.2,
      "end": 915.08,
      "text": "Whoever you are, sir, wherever you are, sir,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 915.2,
      "end": 918.0,
      "text": "Susan A. Lightfoot would love to hear from you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 918.32,
      "end": 919.72,
      "text": "But I'm not giving you the phone number.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 922.9,
      "end": 925.42,
      "text": "Amanda and Karen, who are up there in Glasgow,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 927.24,
      "end": 931.04,
      "text": "say hello to Stephen and Brian from Come Knockin' Ayrshire,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 931.36,
      "end": 932.74,
      "text": "who they met at the Dio concert.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 933.14,
      "end": 935.82,
      "text": "And also hi to Ali and Mickey, or possibly Mikey.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 935.82,
      "end": 940.56,
      "text": "also Duncan, Diane, and Mahari, and all the Kirky headbangers.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 941.18,
      "end": 943.27,
      "text": "Thank you. This is Foreigner.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 943.27,
      "end": 1075.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1080.0,
      "end": 1361.92,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1359.33,
      "end": 1362.47,
      "text": "A definite understatement, but they really were an excellent band.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1363.07,
      "end": 1364.0,
      "text": "Were they not?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1366.92,
      "end": 1371.44,
      "text": "That was Gillen, and the single was called Mutually Assured Destruction.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1375.57,
      "end": 1379.19,
      "text": "It was especially for Ian and Hodgie and Hawkey and Big Stephen Willie.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1380.36,
      "end": 1384.3,
      "text": "A very special hello to a lady by the name of Glynn from Phil Drew,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1384.3,
      "end": 1386.56,
      "text": "who's studying at St. Mary's Medical School, London.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1387.0,
      "end": 1387.98,
      "text": "Probably broken up now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1388.44,
      "end": 1391.83,
      "text": "And before Gillum, you heard Foreigner from their new album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1391.93,
      "end": 1393.81,
      "text": "which is called Argent Provocateur.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1394.67,
      "end": 1396.15,
      "text": "The track we played you was Tooth & Nail.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1396.29,
      "end": 1399.79,
      "text": "That was for all the mates of a fellow by the name of Andy Menin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1400.71,
      "end": 1403.73,
      "text": "Of 11D, Barnard's Yard and Norwich.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1406.3,
      "end": 1408.76,
      "text": "Happy 16th birthday to a fellow by the name of David.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1409.4,
      "end": 1412.46,
      "text": "It's his birthday today from a lady called Amanda, rather.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1412.62,
      "end": 1413.1,
      "text": "Not Monda.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1413.64,
      "end": 1414.82,
      "text": "Getting too French in me old age.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1415.2,
      "end": 1418.1,
      "text": "Amanda, who lives in Wallingford, which is alongside the River Thames",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1418.1,
      "end": 1420.52,
      "text": "and it's got lots of lovely weeping willows, I recollect.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1422.11,
      "end": 1423.81,
      "text": "Also, hello to Lisa Ranger,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1424.85,
      "end": 1427.29,
      "text": "studying at the Birmingham School of Music,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1427.53,
      "end": 1431.03,
      "text": "and to Ben Jones, who is reading Japanese at Sheffield,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1431.67,
      "end": 1435.53,
      "text": "from Mega Maggot Mike.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1437.49,
      "end": 1439.45,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1439.65,
      "end": 1442.39,
      "text": "28 and a half minutes past ten, this is TKO.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1442.85,
      "end": 1448.85,
      "text": "Before that, you heard TKO from a really good album,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1448.85,
      "end": 1795.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1800.0,
      "end": 1911.01,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1910.72,
      "end": 1912.74,
      "text": "which is entitled In Your Face.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1913.89,
      "end": 1916.01,
      "text": "Just been released in this country on Music for Nations,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1916.01,
      "end": 1923.58,
      "text": "the track of lady was called end of the line highly recommend the album good band there is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1923.58,
      "end": 1927.5,
      "text": "a lady by the name of helen burgess who for quite a while it seems we're now with a fellow by the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1927.5,
      "end": 1935.24,
      "text": "name of marco whose address is the markshire golf club ascot quite a long letter but to pray see it",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1935.24,
      "end": 1942.16,
      "text": "helen i think he misses you quite a lot and he wants to stay friends with him nice card this is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1942.16,
      "end": 1947.5,
      "text": "it's all the way from bangor county down northern ireland and it's a request for a fellow by the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1947.5,
      "end": 1953.67,
      "text": "name of simon denley who was 18 on the 14th of this month happy birthday for them and also hello",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1953.67,
      "end": 1960.6,
      "text": "to joe bryson who is the world's greatest brian may freak and hello to anybody who has it says",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1960.6,
      "end": 1986.85,
      "text": "here the great misfortune to know a lady by the name of rachel it is 22 and a half minutes to 11",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1986.85,
      "end": 1991.15,
      "text": "of the clock have a listen to the playing on this track bob dylan let's face it is a one-off but",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1991.15,
      "end": 1995.07,
      "text": "just listen to the guitar, it's really tasty, and it's by an English fella.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1995.07,
      "end": 2155.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2079.74,
      "end": 2089.94,
      "text": "from their double album who's last now before that something from a new live album has just",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2160.0,
      "end": 2952.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2952.02,
      "end": 2954.04,
      "text": "come out by Bob Dylan. The album is called",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2954.04,
      "end": 2956.02,
      "text": "called, well, The Real Live.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2956.78,
      "end": 2958.36,
      "text": "The track was I and I. The guitarist",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2958.36,
      "end": 2960.18,
      "text": "was Mick Taylor, ex of the Rolling Stones",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2960.18,
      "end": 2961.52,
      "text": "and a few other good bands.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2962.02,
      "end": 2963.8,
      "text": "Had a bit of a problem for a while, but now he's",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2963.8,
      "end": 2965.14,
      "text": "obviously well on course.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2968.71,
      "end": 2970.21,
      "text": "Message here to a fellow by the name of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2970.21,
      "end": 2972.81,
      "text": "Tar Pots. That is his nickname.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2973.29,
      "end": 2974.89,
      "text": "He's in Ashford, in Middlesex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2975.59,
      "end": 2976.29,
      "text": "Happy Christmas",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2976.29,
      "end": 2978.71,
      "text": "from me and a mother who",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2978.71,
      "end": 2979.25,
      "text": "cares.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2980.4,
      "end": 2981.32,
      "text": "And he makes as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2982.65,
      "end": 2984.01,
      "text": "Two red hot numbers",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2984.01,
      "end": 2991.05,
      "text": "wish all the cadets over 17 from the acf in clyde bank a dan stinger of a christmas and of course",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2991.05,
      "end": 2997.61,
      "text": "wishing jerry davey steve murray and his bike and all of the pine trees lounge a hell-raising festive",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2997.61,
      "end": 3008.76,
      "text": "season from two red hot numbers a christmas mention here to the radford rock appreciation",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3008.76,
      "end": 3020.65,
      "text": "society namely uncle p and big brother this boxing day there's a chance to have one of the best",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3020.65,
      "end": 3025.69,
      "text": "concerts of the year recorded at london's dominion theater and starring huey lewis and the news",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3053.1,
      "end": 3057.98,
      "text": "yes huey lewis and the news together with the tower of power horns in concert for an hour and",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3057.98,
      "end": 3077.83,
      "text": "25 minutes this boxing day at 5 35 on radio 1 and stereo fm don't miss it it's four minutes to 11.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3077.83,
      "end": 3089.83,
      "text": "here are hanoi rocks a band who don't know too much about them at all other than the fact that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3089.83,
      "end": 3629.22,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3628.79,
      "end": 3634.22,
      "text": "their single is out on official records and they've got a very good reviewing quang they",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3634.22,
      "end": 3639.48,
      "text": "They are called Virgin Star, a single entitled When the Reds, out on official records.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3639.9,
      "end": 3643.64,
      "text": "Before that, you heard Hanoi Rocks, and my repeat session by them recorded it last July.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3643.78,
      "end": 3645.28,
      "text": "The track was Underwater World.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3645.54,
      "end": 3647.14,
      "text": "This is Brian Adams.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3647.66,
      "end": 3655.46,
      "text": "The album is not going to be released here in the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3655.46,
      "end": 3775.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3780.0,
      "end": 4078.4,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4078.4,
      "end": 4080.38,
      "text": "It's on release in America and also in Canada.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4080.62,
      "end": 4083.02,
      "text": "Guess you can get it maybe in an import shop.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4083.14,
      "end": 4084.8,
      "text": "It is out on Atlantic Records.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4085.89,
      "end": 4088.61,
      "text": "It is the first album by a fellow called John Parr.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4088.61,
      "end": 4090.95,
      "text": "The track was entitled Treat Me Like I Am.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4090.95,
      "end": 4095.71,
      "text": "And before that, a track from an album that's coming out at the end of January.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4097.89,
      "end": 4102.19,
      "text": "An album that hasn't got one bad track on it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4103.25,
      "end": 4104.31,
      "text": "By a fellow called Brian Adams.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4104.51,
      "end": 4105.65,
      "text": "The album is called Reckless.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4105.87,
      "end": 4107.53,
      "text": "The track was entitled The Kids Wanna Rock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4117.12,
      "end": 4122.66,
      "text": "Freebird, your old lady Misty is thinking of you back in Beeston, Leeds.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4125.18,
      "end": 4128.02,
      "text": "Tommy Grogan, hello, from Mandy of Rochdale.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4128.42,
      "end": 4133.99,
      "text": "Tommy Grogan, hello, from Lynn, also of Rochdale.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4134.21,
      "end": 4134.79,
      "text": "Lucky boy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4138.14,
      "end": 4140.18,
      "text": "Warren, welcome back from Bangladesh.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4143.0,
      "end": 4145.44,
      "text": "Best wishes from me, and also from Medellin.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4145.8,
      "end": 4146.42,
      "text": "You know her.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4168.47,
      "end": 4170.61,
      "text": "Recognize these chords from UFO?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4171.47,
      "end": 4177.47,
      "text": "We did a session with them about two years ago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4177.47,
      "end": 4315.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4320.0,
      "end": 4786.38,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4786.38,
      "end": 4787.84,
      "text": "Actually, three years ago now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4789.73,
      "end": 4792.01,
      "text": "And now they've finally got themselves a really good record deal",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4792.01,
      "end": 4793.13,
      "text": "with a major record company.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4793.25,
      "end": 4793.81,
      "text": "Good luck to them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4793.87,
      "end": 4794.61,
      "text": "They're stuck at it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4794.69,
      "end": 4795.71,
      "text": "They're called Terraplane.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4796.19,
      "end": 4797.09,
      "text": "That's a single that's out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4797.15,
      "end": 4798.55,
      "text": "It's called I Can't Live Without Your Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4798.59,
      "end": 4799.09,
      "text": "Good band.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4799.37,
      "end": 4801.77,
      "text": "Prior to that, a classic from a classic album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4801.77,
      "end": 4805.11,
      "text": "Released in 1977, the album is called Lights Out.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4806.2,
      "end": 4807.36,
      "text": "The band, UFO.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4807.74,
      "end": 4808.9,
      "text": "The track, Love to Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4812.7,
      "end": 4815.38,
      "text": "Lady by the name of Kay lives at, or in,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4815.68,
      "end": 4817.98,
      "text": "Millbourne Port, Zommerzett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4820.12,
      "end": 4822.36,
      "text": "Requires a mention for somebody who lives at",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4822.36,
      "end": 4824.24,
      "text": "Barmby Moor near York,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4824.72,
      "end": 4825.86,
      "text": "a fellow by the name of James.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4826.56,
      "end": 4828.62,
      "text": "Message to James goes like this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4828.68,
      "end": 4829.26,
      "text": "Hope you're well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4829.48,
      "end": 4830.6,
      "text": "Lots of love to all the family.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4831.18,
      "end": 4834.22,
      "text": "And I'll wave when our trains pass next October.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4834.64,
      "end": 4835.85,
      "text": "Hello, James.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4836.07,
      "end": 4836.43,
      "text": "Hello, Kay.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4837.94,
      "end": 4840.86,
      "text": "Debbie Mayo lives in Shrewsbury, Shropshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4841.85,
      "end": 4845.43,
      "text": "Message here for her ex-fiancé, Darren Garner.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4848.06,
      "end": 4849.48,
      "text": "Darren, I've just got to say this to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4849.72,
      "end": 4851.54,
      "text": "She says, I am still thinking about you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4852.12,
      "end": 4854.5,
      "text": "Thank you very much for the four years that we had together.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4855.0,
      "end": 4856.52,
      "text": "I'll get in touch.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4858.2,
      "end": 4863.0,
      "text": "Hanoi rocks on their album, which is called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4863.0,
      "end": 5335.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5336.64,
      "end": 5339.06,
      "text": "And the Cannons of Destruction Have Begun.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5339.2,
      "end": 5340.54,
      "text": "I sincerely hope they haven't.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5340.94,
      "end": 5342.3,
      "text": "The track was called Aliens.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5342.52,
      "end": 5345.32,
      "text": "Before that, Hanoi rocks on the Boulevard of Broken Dreams.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5345.74,
      "end": 5347.4,
      "text": "26 and a half minutes now to 12.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5347.4,
      "end": 5349.72,
      "text": "This is the Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5350.2,
      "end": 5351.82,
      "text": "This fella, who plays the guitar on this track,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5351.88,
      "end": 5353.52,
      "text": "is a guy by the name of Jan Ackerman.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5353.9,
      "end": 5355.2,
      "text": "He used to be in Focus.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5355.5,
      "end": 5357.68,
      "text": "He's been making solo albums since about 1974.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5358.16,
      "end": 5359.24,
      "text": "He is utterly brilliant.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5359.42,
      "end": 5362.08,
      "text": "This is from his new album, which is called From the Basement.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5362.26,
      "end": 5364.26,
      "text": "Jan Ackerman, a headbanger.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}